two camera_orbit_* values. +yaw = orbiting to higher than center, -yaw = orbiting to lower than center, +pitch = orbiting to the right side of center, -pitch = orbiting to the left side of center. I find +/-1.0 degree in any orbit axis to be a meaningful limit, too much orbiting off-center and you start seeing a ton of gaussian splatting reconstruction artifacts.\n\nThe rest you can keep default, or fiddle around."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"BASIC GUIDE:\n\n* I'd keep focal length 35mm (works well most footage).\n\n* For custom_baseline_mm, enter your IPD ideally, for most people its somewhere between 50-75mm.\n\n* custom_convergence_m dictates how close/far the objects in the scene feel to your eyes, in VR i find 3 meters (3.0 here) to feel best for stereoscopy 3D effect of shots with people. Too low = eye-strain. Too high = weaker 3D effect.\n\n* You can dolly in a bit closer to the center of the scene with the camera_dolly_m value. I find +0.05 m to be a meaningful limit, too much dolly-in and you're just getting too close and clipping into geometry of the center objects.\n\n* You can orbit off-center around the center of the scene left/right/higher/lower with the two camera_orbit_* values. +yaw = orbiting to higher than center, -yaw = orbiting to lower than center, +pitch = orbiting to the right side of center, -pitch = orbiting to the left side of center. I find +/-1.0 degree in any orbit axis to be a meaningful limit, too much orbiting off-center and you start seeing a ton of gaussian splatting reconstruction artifacts.\n\nThe rest you can keep default, or fiddle around."},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":17,"type":"Note","pos":[-1417.3109517062755,5705.984794902521],"size":[296.8432032364883,189.1930336689611],"flags":{},"order":2,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["NOTE: \n\nif input video has an audio track as well, be sure to connect the audio-out from Load Video (Upload) VHS node, directly to audio(in) for the Video Combine VHS node, so the audio stays muxed in the output video."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"NOTE: \n\nif input video has an audio track as well, be sure to connect the audio-out from Load Video (Upload) VHS node, directly to audio(in) for the Video Combine VHS node, so the audio stays muxed in the output video."},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"}],"links":[[4,7,0,4,0,"SHARP_VR_VIDEO_MODEL_CONFIG"],[7,4,0,9,0,"IMAGE"],[8,2,3,6,0,"VHS_VIDEOINFO"],[9,6,0,9,4,"FLOAT"],[11,2,0,4,1,"IMAGE"]],"groups":[],"config":{},"extra":{"ds":{"scale":0.8390545288824117,"offset":[1765.3152535177237,-4774.2386774433835]}},"version":0.4}